    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic is making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a worn one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a continuous loop of rubber that drives essential accessories like the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor using energy from your engine. A worn belt often becomes brittle and develops cracks or glazing, which causes it to slip off its pulleys under load instead of gripping them tightly. This slipping creates the characteristic high-pitched squealing noise you hear when accelerating because the friction needed to grip the engine components is lost. Addressing this immediately is crucial, as a failing belt can permanently damage your engine or electrical systems.",
